Mutation for scripts/joint.sh section C (B5-02, A2A-DESIGN SI-1 "关闭加密"): the sealed envelope's
ciphertext is its plaintext. Seal writes the padded, signed inner message followed by a zero "tag" of
the AEAD's length, and Open strips it; the HPKE key agreement still runs (the ack_key is still
exported), so envelopes keep their shape,
every daemon built with it still understands every other, and the hub (which never opens an envelope)
accepts them. Everything that crosses the hub is readable there. Never commit it applied.

Repository: ANetCore
Expect: SI-1 canary hits

Apply and run with scripts/mutations/mutate.sh (it copies the three working trees to a scratch
directory, applies the patch there and builds the joint binary set from the copy):

    scripts/mutations/mutate.sh canary scripts/mutations/si1-plaintext-envelope.patch

or, for a test host without go:

    scripts/mutations/mutate.sh build -o "$MUTBIN" scripts/mutations/si1-plaintext-envelope.patch
    JOINT_BIN="$MUTBIN" JOINT_CANARY_ONLY=1 J=/tmp/jx scripts/joint.sh   # on the host
    scripts/mutations/mutate.sh check /tmp/jx

Expected: section C red. Every goal, chat turn, attachment and argument crosses the hub in the clear,
so the tap's record of the canary nodes' hub traffic holds each canary (base64 in /relay/send bodies and
/relay/poll answers), and the hub's data directory usually does too (relay rows until they are
acknowledged; their pages in the WAL after). The recipients still read everything back, and the
settlement check stays green: the payment objects never carried content. Unit level: the seal tests
that open with real HPKE or expect a wrong key to fail (TestOpenRecipientAndKey, TestSEALED_2A, …).

